    "growth_rate_source": "Blend of revenue 3yr CAGR (3.9%, post-FLIR organic-plus-bolt-on) and FY2026 guidance (+6.8%), backed by ~$5.0B funded backlog and book-to-bill >1.0 for 11 quarters. Equity CAGR rejected as the anchor: 5yr is inflated by the FLIR share issuance.",
    "growth_divergence_warning": "Equity 5yr CAGR 26.6% diverges >30% from revenue (14.6%) and EPS (11.8%) -- driven by ~$4B of stock issued for FLIR in FY2021, not retained earnings. 5yr revenue/EPS CAGRs also embed FLIR and are not organic.",
    "notes": "Owner FCF = reported FCF - SBC (interest income not stripped; net debt). Owner FCF: FY2020 517.5, FY2022 362.7, FY2025 1,034.4. The 3yr FCF CAGR (41.8%) is an artefact of a depressed FY2022 base (tax on divestitures and Sec.174 cash taxes) and is not a growth signal. Owner-FCF 5yr CAGR (14.9%) is slightly ABOVE reported (14.4%): SBC grew slower than cash flow, so no SBC-funded growth concern."
  },
  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "Teledyne delivers the raised FY2026 outlook (>$6.53B, +6.8% including acquired DD-Scientific and full-year Excelitas A&D), then grows mid-single digits as the ~$5.0B funded backlog and 11 straight quarters of book-to-bill >1.0 convert, with Digital Imaging's space, unmanned and counter-UAS lines (>10% growth) offsetting flat Instrumentation and Engineered Systems. Growth fades to 3% by year 8 as the defense budget step-up normalises. Pre-SBC EBITDA margin edges from 25.4% to 26.5% on mix and FLIR integration leverage, roughly the H1-2026 run-rate plus one point, well inside the 27-28% peers like AMETEK earn. Acquired-intangible amortization rolls off, so the D&A tax shield fades and cash tax settles at ~23.5%. Varex and future bolt-ons are excluded on the view that Teledyne pays fair prices.",
    "bull": "The proposed ~$1.5T FY2027 US defense budget and allied rearmament make the current order surge (Q2-2026 orders +20%, Digital Imaging book-to-bill 1.4x) a multi-year step-up rather than a spike: FLIR thermal, counter-UAS, space-qualified sensors and unmanned systems drive 7-8.5% organic growth for four years, industrial machine-vision and marine instrumentation recover, and operating leverage plus vertical integration in infrared lift pre-SBC EBITDA margin to 28%. Terminal growth 3% and a 20x cap reflect a durable niche-compounder with qualified/sole-source positions.",
    "bear": "FY2026 lands short of guidance as H2 industrial demand softens, then the bear axes compound: US export controls and entity-list restrictions cut China (a top-five international market) sales of dual-use thermal and imaging products, tariffs raise semiconductor and optics input costs, Instrumentation and machine-vision follow global industrial capex down, and the defense budget plateaus under continuing resolutions after the 2026-27 surge. Revenue grows only 1-1.5% in years 2-3 and pre-SBC EBITDA margin falls to 23.5% before recovering to 24% -- roughly the FY2022-24 GAAP-equivalent range. Terminal growth 2%, 15x cap for a slower, more cyclical conglomerate. Leadership continuity (Mehrabian's contract expires December 2026) adds execution risk to the M&A machine."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Teledyne is valued as a diversified, moderately cyclical sensor/instrumentation/defense-electronics operating company on strict owner FCF: SBC (small, ~0.65% of revenue) expensed with a flat diluted share count, components built per year rather than carrying the FY2025 FCF margin forward, acquired-intangible amortization allowed to roll off so its tax shield is not perpetuated, and growth limited to the organic business -- pending Varex and future bolt-on M&A are excluded on both sides of the ledger.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Serial M&A is the core of the historical growth record; excluding it understates growth if Teledyne keeps buying below intrinsic value, and overstates value if it overpays (Varex ~$1.1B pending).",
      "US export controls on China (top-five international market) for dual-use thermal/imaging products.",
      "Defense/space budget timing: the order surge may be a peak, not a step-up.",
      "Industrial/instrumentation cyclicality in roughly half of revenue.",
      "Terminal value is the majority of EV; WACC +/-1pp moves value materially (see sensitivity grid)."
    ]
  },
