    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF (operating company, US filer, moderately cyclical diversified industrial/defense electronics). Routed via dcf-methods SKILL.md row 1/2; adaptations considered but none bind beyond lease consistency and cyclical-cap discipline (USD flows, USD quote, no NCI, SBC non-zero). FY0 = FY2025 (revenue $6,115.4M). Year 1 = FY2026 guidance (raised July 2026 to >$6.53B, +6.8%, includes full-year Excelitas A&D/DD-Scientific acquired revenue). ADJ EBITDA is pre-SBC: FY2025 operating income 1,149.8 + D&A 336.3 + SBC 39.6 = 1,525.7 (24.9%); H1-2026 = 627.4 + 172.9 + 19.5 = 819.8 (25.4%). D&A includes $216.6M of acquired-intangible amortization (3.5% of revenue) which rolls off over the horizon; the D&A path glides from 5.4% to 2.3% so the terminal year does not perpetuate an amortization tax shield (terminal D&A ~ depreciation ~ capex). Cash tax on EBIT: FY2025 cash taxes paid $280.2M / EBIT $1,149.8M = 24.4%, FY2024 21.6%, FY2023 30% (Sec.174 R&D capitalisation); the 2025 OBBBA restoration of domestic R&D expensing lowers near-term cash tax, so the path is 22% in FY2026 rising to 23.5%. Working capital: manufacturer with receivables+inventory > payables, so wc_capture is NEGATIVE (-10% of incremental revenue). BUYBACKS: $402.9M in FY2025, $354.0M FY2024, only $2.9M H1-2026 (capital going to debt paydown and M&A) -- the flat share count is funded intermittently. PENDING VAREX IMAGING ACQUISITION (~$1.1B cash, $18.90/sh, close expected early 2027) is NOT modelled: it is unclosed, debt/cash funded and assumed priced at roughly fair value, so it is value-neutral to a first approximation; on close it adds ~$1.1B to net debt and ~$0.85B of revenue. Unmodelled serial M&A is likewise excluded (its growth is excluded together with its cost). Interest income is not stripped (TDY is net debt). Price is a regular-session close.",
